WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.060
After decades of Freddy Krueger movies, it's
easy to forget where this killer came from

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:06.680
and why he became so iconic.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.440
So we're taking a deep dive into the man behind
the third-degree burns.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.860
From his monstrous conception to his showdown
with Jason, here's Freddy Krueger's backstory

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.560
explained.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.019
Things were never going to be easy for Frederick
Charles Krueger.

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:24.630
As chronicled in A Nightmare On Elm Street
3: Dream Warriors, his mother, Amanda Krueger,

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.909
was better known by her chosen name, Sister
Mary Helena.

00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:32.120
"It is an abomination to God and to man."

00:00:32.309 --> 00:00:36.359
As a nun, she worked at the Hathaway House,
an asylum for the criminally deranged.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.580
A few days before Christmas 1941, Amanda found
herself the victim of a mix-up.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.280
She was locked inside the building when the
guards went home for the long weekend, leaving

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.380
the high-security hospital unattended.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.449
By the time she was found, she'd suffered
a series of horrendous attacks at the hands

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:53.520
of the inmates and was pregnant with:

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:57.440
"The bastard son of a hundred maniacs."

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.540
Nine months later, a bouncing baby Freddy
was born.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.560
Never one to catch a break, he was adopted
by an abusive alcoholic named Mr. Underwood.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.520
What followed was, predictably, sort of a
huge nightmare.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.400
Understandably, Freddy was a troubled child.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.960
His adopted dad was drunk all the time and
seemed to take a great deal of joy in beating

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.320
his young ward with a belt.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.500
At school, Freddy was taunted mercilessly
for his heritage.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.680
"Son of a hundred maniacs!

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.600
Son of a hundred maniacs!

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:26.980
Son of a hundred maniacs!"

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.220
He started to exhibit the telltale signs of
a fictional serial killer, killing the class

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.100
hamster and getting a kick out of cutting
himself with a straight razor.

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:40.280
Sadly, young Frederick never experienced a
personal metamorphosis, and on one particularly

00:01:40.299 --> 00:01:45.290
unfortunate day, unable to stomach the constant
tirade of abuse from his adoptive dad, Freddy

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:49.079
jammed his razor blade deep into the eye socket
of his father figure.

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:53.399
It could be argued that this was where any
hopes of a happy life died, and the Springwood

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.640
Slasher was born.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:58.940
The events of Freddy's young adult life are
murky, and it's not clear whether or not he

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:02.280
ever faced any legal consequences for killing
Mr. Underwood.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.520
What is known is that by his mid-20s, Fred
Krueger was in the family way.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.560
He'd married a woman named Loretta who gave
birth to a daughter, Katherine.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.110
Together, they lived what was, to the casual
observer, a simple, happy, family life.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:18.140
Lying just beneath the surface, however, was
a dark secret.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:23.040
Freddy, unable to stem his unquenchable bloodlust,
had constructed a secret room in the family's

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:23.980
suburban home.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:29.060
Inside, he kept a series of homemade weapons,
newspaper clippings, and memorabilia from

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:33.760
his off-hours hobby, which was slaughtering
the children of Springwood, Ohio, as the mysterious

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.090
killer known as the Springwood Slasher.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.960
"But I made 'em pay.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.940
I took all their children away from them."

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.680
Marriage is, if nothing else, based on trust,
and the Kruegers' home life hit a speed bump

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.280
when Loretta discovered Freddy's macabre man
cave.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.000
Freddy killed his wife in front of their young
daughter, was later arrested for the deaths

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.340
of numerous local children, and Katherine
was put into foster care under a new name.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.480
The arrest and subsequent trial of Fred Krueger
sparked high tempers in the good folks of

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:05.080
Springwood.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:09.380
The evidence condemning the Springwood Slasher
was damning, and justice for the roughly two

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.700
dozen children who died by his beknifed hand
lay on the line.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.220
Unfortunately, thanks to a misplaced signature
and a drunken judge, Krueger was set free

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.940
despite clearly being guilty.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:24.080
"Oh, the lawyers got fat and the judge got
famous, but somebody forgot to sign the search

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:26.760
warrant in the right place, and Krueger was
free, just like that."

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:30.620
The parents of Springwood, however, were less
than inclined to follow suit.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.290
The good folks of Springwood formed an old-fashioned
vigilante mob, trapping Fred and soaking him

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.470
in gasoline before lighting him on fire.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.940
Little did they know that as they watched
the building burn to the ground, Krueger was

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.700
being approached by Dream Demons.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:47.480
These supernatural entities offered Krueger
the opportunity to carry on his sadistic ways

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:50.660
indefinitely as their otherworldly, antagonistic
agent.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.300
"We know what you want."

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.760
"I want it all!"

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:55.980
"Of course you do."

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:56.980
"Then open up."

00:03:57.020 --> 00:04:00.360
"And you shall be forever!"

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:05.300
Krueger became a denizen of the Dream Realm,
a plane of existence where human subconscious

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.400
thought takes place.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.211
While there, he had the ability to manipulate
reality and affect unconscious humans, as

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.000
long as he was still remembered and feared
in the real world.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:16.980
His control over the dream world seemed just
about unlimited.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:22.440
He could change his shape, move objects telepathically,
and warp the physical manifestations of dreamers.

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:26.860
Additionally, any damage that Freddy caused
in a dream also happened in the real world.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.680
Blended into a geyser of blood and viscera
in your nightmare?

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:34.070
Your parents are in for a double dose of tragedy
as your death goes unexplained, and they never

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:36.540
to resell your otherwise lightly used mattress.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:41.880
Being on the Dream Demon payroll has plenty
of pluses, but it's not without some downsides.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:46.270
For one, you're pretty well stuck in the Dream
Realm, a supernatural blend of the collective

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:46.860
unconscious.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:51.640
Re-entering the physical plane leads to nothing
but trouble for Mr. Krueger, who becomes susceptible

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.040
to pain and even death.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.520
"Kids."

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.960
In the meantime, life in the Dream Realm can
be every bit as frustrating.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:05.480
Generally speaking, Freddy can only consume
the souls of the residents of Springwood,

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:06.760
barring outside intervention.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:11.099
Even then, the powers only work when the good
folks of Springwood harbor a healthy level

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.120
of active fear regarding Elm Street's favorite
burn victim.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.500
If nobody remembers Freddy, he's nothing more
than a bad dream.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.800
"Being dead wasn't a problem.

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:20.600
But being forgotten?

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.680
Now that's a b----."

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.800
Thirteen years after his unholy baptism by
fire, Freddy made his first known appearance

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.930
in the form we've all come to know and lose
sleep over in A Nightmare on Elm Street.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.180
With his sick new menagerie of superpowers,
he began to haunt the dreams of the children

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:36.940
of Springwood.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.960
With vengeance for his death and skullduggery
in his heart, he got down to the business

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.380
of gruesome child killing.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:47.000
The first to go was Tina, who started off
the story proper with a bad dream about a

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.880
disfigured, claw-handed man pursuing her through
a boiler room.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:54.560
Tina made the age-old mistake of being a romantically
active teenager in a horror film, and she

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.330
paid for it in the form of a dream world glove-slashing.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:02.389
Freddy would go on to drop Rod, Tina's boyfriend,
with a swift strangulation, as well as Glen,

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:03.720
our hero Nancy's beau.

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:07.540
Nancy, meanwhile, managed to beat back the
nefarious killer, using nothing but her wit

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.440
and her will.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:12.680
"I take back every bit of energy I gave you.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.180
You're nothing."

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.480
Or did she?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:20.440
At the end of the film, she certainly seemed
to lose out while Krueger played evil Knight

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:20.940
Rider.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:25.420
If the ending of A Nightmare On Elm Street
was strange, the entirety of A Nightmare On

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:28.580
Elm Street 2: Freddy's Revenge was on a whole
different level.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:32.419
The rules that had held sway in the first
film disappeared, and Freddy became a little

00:06:32.419 --> 00:06:36.749
less dream monster and, for one brief entry
in the franchise, a little more of a metaphor

00:06:36.749 --> 00:06:39.680
for repressed romantic feelings between teenage
boys.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:42.200
"Something is trying to get inside my body."

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:44.520
"Yeah, and she's female and she's waiting
for you in the cabana.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:45.780
And you want to sleep with me."

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:50.140
The main character, Jesse, was an adolescent
boy who moved into Nancy's old house on Elm

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:50.720
Street.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:54.900
Rather than haunting the kid's dreams, Krueger
would straight-up possess the lad, eventually

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:58.710
taking over his body and physically manifesting
in his burned-up form.

00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:03.060
The forces of something eventually won the
day, and Freddy was sent back to the unconscious

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:03.560
realm.

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:07.840
It's certainly a cult classic, but not necessarily
a classic classic.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:13.279
Krueger was back to his old shenanigans in
A Nightmare On Elm Street 3: Dream Warriors.

00:07:13.279 --> 00:07:17.150
All of the children of Elm Street had either
been killed or driven mad, with the survivors

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.660
living together in an asylum.

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:20.140
Only, there was a twist!

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.279
The residents of the asylum were brought together
by none other than Nancy Thompson from the

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:28.540
first movie, now working in the hospital while
researching dreams for graduate school.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.900
One of the patients, young Kristen Parker,
had the ability to pull other people into

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.740
her dreams, where the folks inside were granted
superpowers.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.720
"Nancy!"

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:51.219
Freddy, it turned out, could be defeated if
his bones were buried and sanctified, which

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.140
was something the good guys learned from the
ghost of his dead mother.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.540
Freddy wound up down for the count thanks
to a hasty burial, and nobody ever heard from

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.040
him again.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.280
Only they did.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:05.580
A Nightmare On Elm Street 4: The Dream Master
saw Freddy's return, as Nightmare On Elm Street

00:08:05.581 --> 00:08:06.919
sequels usually do.

00:08:06.919 --> 00:08:11.469
Here, he bounced back in a big way and put
down all of those pesky kids from Dream Warriors

00:08:11.469 --> 00:08:14.300
like he was living some Scooby Doo villain's
power fantasy.

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:19.879
He was taken down by Alice Johnson, a teenage
sleep messiah and, quote, "Dream Master" capable

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.820
of manipulating good dreams the way Freddy
controlled the bad.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.680
"How do you handle your nightmares?"

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:27.080
"My mom taught me, when I was little.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:30.880
Did you ever hear of the Dream Master?"

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.640
But you can't keep a good son of a hundred
maniacs down, and Freddy, confusingly, birthed

00:08:35.650 --> 00:08:39.390
himself from the spirit of his dead mother
in the fifth film, The Dream Child.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:44.190
He then tried possessing Alice's unborn baby,
but he wound up reverting back to infancy

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:46.420
and was re-absorbed by his ghost mom.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.260
All of which brings us to Freddy's Dead: The
Final Nightmare.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:54.200
Set years after the previous films in a Biff
Tannen-esque future where Freddy finally achieved

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.420
his goals, the movie takes place in a Springwood
devoid of youth thanks to the knife-handed

00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:58.920
maniac.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:03.000
By the time the credits rolled, Freddy was
reunited with his long-lost daughter, who

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.040
pulled him into the physical world and gave
him a thorough stabbing, sending Krueger to

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:08.440
Hell once and for all.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:09.380
Ish.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:14.760
These days, any brand-friendly fictional character
worth their salt has been revamped, rebooted,

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.300
and re-imagined at least half a dozen times.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:21.240
Freddy Krueger managed to get a head start
on the trend with the decidedly bananas Wes

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.720
Craven's New Nightmare.

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:27.580
Released in 1994, back when fourth walls were
still considered to be generally load bearing,

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.470
New Nightmare posited that an embodiment of
evil could be contained within the essence

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.710
of a fictional character, and that the concept
of Freddy Krueger had become the home of one

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:36.710
such entity.

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:41.040
Within the film, this supernatural force broke
free of the confines of the fictional world,

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.370
wreaking havoc on the production of a proposed
new Nightmare on Elm Street entry and attacking

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:47.930
the real-world people involved in creating
the series.

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:52.220
"He's been held captive pretty much as Freddy
in the Nightmare on Elm Street series, but

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:57.080
now that the films have ended, the genie's
out of the bottle."

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:58.000
Bonkers?

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.160
Totally, and maybe a little less relatable
than the relatively straightforward agent

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.500
of ancient nightmare demons that audiences
had become accustomed to.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:10.260
A monster is only as good as its over-the-top
smackdowns, and Freddy Krueger has a decent

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.840
history of playing king of the hill with other
fictional freak shows.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.410
The most famous of these came in the form
of 2003's Freddy vs. Jason, the critically

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.500
panned but long-awaited cross promotional
extravaganza.

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:25.140
If things went just a little bit differently,
Freddy would've had a whole new fight on his

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.380
unwieldy knife hands.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:30.580
According to the screenwriters on Freddy vs.
Jason, one potential ending that was scrapped

00:10:30.580 --> 00:10:35.310
over rights issues involved Krueger and Jason
in Hell together being taunted by Pinhead

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:36.640
of the Hellraiser series.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:40.570
Luckily enough for fans who felt like there
was beef left unsquashed by the crossover,

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:45.750
a sequel comic was released a few years later,
and it added the one thing that can, mathematically,

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:49.270
only improve on as a product sprinkled in
liberally: Bruce Campbell.

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:54.300
The 2007 mini series Freddy vs. Jason vs.
Ash is difficult not to love.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:11:00.920
Out from the self-aware '90s and the kind-of-a-drag
early 2000s came the dark age of gritty, ill-received

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:01.420
reboots.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.500
And lo, there was 2010's A Nightmare On Elm
Street.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:08.320
Jumping in at the tail end of that couple
of years when superheroes weren't quite 100

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:11.940
percent viable money printing machines and
nostalgia still seemed like the Hollywood

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:16.140
team to beat, the Nightmare on Elm Street
reboot had all of the hallmarks of its time.

00:11:16.140 --> 00:11:20.280
Heavily color filtered, devoid of comic relief,
and starring a lead actor who was probably

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.900
too good for the material, it spoke its truth.

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:27.260
"Hey," it seemed to say to the world, "what
if Freddy Krueger, generally the only person

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:32.120
in these movies who seems to be having a good
time, was just gross and creepy and looked

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.270
like a ghoul from Fallout 3?"

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:37.240
"How's this for a wet dream?"

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:40.500
And audiences responded with a mighty "who
cares?"

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.780
The movie was a box office disappointment,
and it somehow managed to nab a lower Rotten

00:11:44.780 --> 00:11:49.040
Tomatoes score than the great American cash
grab that was Freddy vs. Jason.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:53.000
Positive aspects included some genuinely unsettling
nightmare sequences.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.660
Less defensible points in the film were...pretty
much everything else.

